<v Alex Blumberg>你没理解错。CDO 经理感到困惑，因为投资者 Magnetar 正在向他施压，要求将更高风险的资产放入该投资者自己购买的 CDO 中。这种情况在 Magnetar 的 CDO 中反复发生。还有另一位银行家参与了另一个 Magnetar CDO 的创造，他描述了 Magnetar 和 CDO 经理之间关于资产质量的“反复争斗”，同样，Magnetar 在推动风险更高的资产。还有另一笔交易，争斗发生在邮件中，Jake 和 Jesse 拿到了副本。

00:24:11.560 --> 00:24:41.040
<v Jesse Eisinger>In an email that one Magnetar person wrote in September of 2006 said, "The original portfolio target spreadsheet that I have had a strangely low spread target. That, of course, would not at all be beneficial to us. I've attached the target portfolio that I would like for this deal with target spreads." So basically, in the email, they're saying, these are the kinds of assets we want, and this is how risky we want it to be.
<v Jesse Eisinger>在 2006 年 9 月的一封邮件中，一位 Magnetar 的人写道：“我拥有的原始投资组合目标表有一个奇怪的低利差目标。这当然对我们一点好处都没有。我附上了我想要用于此交易的目标投资组合和目标利差。”所以基本上，在邮件中，他们是在说，这就是我们想要的资产类型，这就是我们想要的风险水平。

00:24:41.040 --> 00:25:06.260
<v Jesse Eisinger>Well, the CDO manager was not terribly excited about this. And he sent an email back rather forcefully saying, "We will not assemble a portfolio we are not proud of and feel strongly about in the name of a spread target." And so the two sides drifted apart and the CDO was never consummated in part because of the CDO manager's concern about Magnetar's need for riskier assets.
